cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use BEAM in your work, please cite it using the metadata below.
title: "BEAM: a computable probability landscape for T cell receptor repertoires"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/MuteJester/BEAM"
url: "https://github.com/MuteJester/BEAM"
abstract: >-
  BEAM is a probability model for T cell receptor beta CDR3 amino-acid
  sequences that combines local sequence dependence with exact normalisation.
  Its tractable local structure permits deterministic evaluation of sequence
  probabilities, the expected recovery, recurrence, overlap and publicness of
  sequences at a given sampling depth, and interpretable distances between
  repertoires, without enumerating or Monte Carlo sampling the space of
  sequences.
keywords:
  - T cell receptor
  - TCR repertoire
  - CDR3
  - AIRR-seq
  - immune repertoire
  - probabilistic model
  - publicness
  - sampling depth
  - repertoire comparison
authors:
